 unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference."}]}]},{"name":"content","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for Time."}]}]},{"name":"number","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff number within the part that this element applies to. If absent, the time signature applies to all staves in the part."}]}]},{"name":"symbol","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol used to indicate common and cut time as well as a single number display."}]}]},{"name":"separator","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"How the beats and beat-type values are displayed relative to one another. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".stacked"},{"text":" if not specified.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"color"},{"name":"halign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"printsObject","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print an object (e.g. a note or a rest). Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" if not specified.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTime\/init(id:content:number:symbol:separator:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsObject:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltime\/init(id:content:number:symbol:separator:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsobject:)"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTimeSymbol":{"title":"MXLTimeSymbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTimeSymbol"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltimesymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The time-symbol type indicates how to display a time signature. The normal value is the usual fractional"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"display, and is the implied symbol type if none is specified. Other options are the common and cut time"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, as well as a single number with an implied denominator. The note symbol indicates that the beat-type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should be represented with the corresponding downstem note rather than a number. The dotted-note symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicates that the beat-type should be represented with a dotted downstem note that corresponds to three times","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the beat-type value, and a numerator that is one third the beats value.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTimeSymbol"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTime/init(id:content:number:symbol:separator:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsObject:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"init(id:content:number:symbol:separator:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsObject:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTime\/init(id:content:number:symbol:separator:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsObject:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltime\/init(id:content:number:symbol:separator:position:font:color:halign:valign:printsobject:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"content"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLTimeV7ContentO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Content"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLStaffNumberV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStaffNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTimeSymbolO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTimeSymbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalPar